{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01333",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 6.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Uh, morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.38,
      "end_seconds": 12.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.44,
      "end_seconds": 21.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Erm, you know, honestly, it's skipped beats, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.39,
      "end_seconds": 32.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.31,
      "end_seconds": 55.4,
      "duration_seconds": 21.09,
      "text": "Ah, honestly, a few times a day. It's severe, honestly. It's worse with caffeine and lying down. I mean, and there's a flutter in my chest as well, three days now. Oh, and being a bit anxious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.92,
      "end_seconds": 61.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Have you had skipped beats before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.37,
      "end_seconds": 71.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.62,
      "end_seconds": 76.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.12,
      "end_seconds": 85.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.41,
      "end_seconds": 107.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 72 beats a minute, BP is 125 over 72, temperature is 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.19,
      "end_seconds": 110.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.24,
      "end_seconds": 112.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.93,
      "end_seconds": 115.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.41,
      "end_seconds": 130.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.2,
      "end_seconds": 131.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.95,
      "end_seconds": 136.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.52,
      "end_seconds": 148.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "So, have you had any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.81,
      "end_seconds": 156.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No. No shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.59,
      "end_seconds": 162.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Okay, any dizziness, chest pain or fainting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.21,
      "end_seconds": 168.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "No dizziness, chest pain or fainting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.7,
      "end_seconds": 175.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.0,
      "end_seconds": 179.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Actually, no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.74,
      "end_seconds": 201.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.15,
      "end_seconds": 212.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "It's apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. It's herbal calming tea, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.91,
      "end_seconds": 215.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.9,
      "end_seconds": 218.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "About about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.68,
      "end_seconds": 223.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.88,
      "end_seconds": 237.89,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. I work in accounts at a hospital. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.54,
      "end_seconds": 242.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Right, any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.88,
      "end_seconds": 247.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Just my womb taken out, fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.39,
      "end_seconds": 252.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.76,
      "end_seconds": 255.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Yes, an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.8,
      "end_seconds": 262.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.01,
      "end_seconds": 265.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.05,
      "end_seconds": 286.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, the most likely explanation is harmless extra heartbeats. Another possibility is an anxiety-related palpitation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.39,
      "end_seconds": 289.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.26,
      "end_seconds": 306.62,
      "duration_seconds": 15.36,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with harmless extra heartbeats do well once it's treated properly. I think an ECG makes sense here, for palpitations. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.61,
      "end_seconds": 313.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Let me think, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}